{
  "caveats": [
    "Every candidate was first proposed by LobbyPlag's own lexical matcher, so verified pairs are lexically similar by construction; this favours BM25 and understates what a meaning signal adds for paraphrase.",
    "One law (GDPR, 2013) and a pool of about 1,000 proposals; recall falls as the pool grows.",
    "LobbyPlag proposals are short edits. The meaning scorers read only a proposal's new wording (its deleted wording when it only deletes), as if it were a passage quoted from a paper.",
    "Negatives are weak: crowd-rejected candidates only; unlabelled candidates are not negatives (bead R1). Positives are mostly verbatim copies, so precision on rewordings is unmeasured.",
    "Embeddings are 8-bit and computed one text per call, since this build's vectors depend on the batch (see services/qwen_onnx.py).",
    "A query that cannot run (empty or over-long text) counts as a miss and is listed in `query_errors`."
  ],
